  "commonNameControlChar": "Un nombre no puede contener un carácter invisible. Péguelo primero en un editor de texto sin formato o escríbalo a mano.",
  "@commonNameControlChar": {
    "description": "Shown when a typed file name holds a C0 control character or DEL - a tab, a newline, or similar. Named separately from commonNameIllegal because that sentence lists the characters it refuses, and these have no printable form to list. A keyboard cannot type one; a paste from a spreadsheet or a web page can carry one in.",
    "placeholders": {}
  },
  "commonNameNonAscii": "El Flipper solo acepta letras inglesas, cifras y signos de puntuación básicos en un nombre.",
  "@commonNameNonAscii": {
    "description": "Shown when a typed file name holds a character outside ASCII. TRANSLATORS: 'English letters' means the unaccented Latin A-Z and a-z, and nothing else - German ß, Cyrillic я and an emoji are all refused, so do not render this as 'letters of the English language' in a way that leaves accented Latin sounding acceptable. 'Basic punctuation' is deliberately vague rather than a list: most ASCII punctuation is fine, and the nine characters that are not are refused by their own message, commonNameIllegal, which carries the list. Say that the Flipper refuses the name, not that the name is invalid - the same name is perfectly fine on the phone, and it is the device that will not carry it.",
    "placeholders": {}
  },
  "commonNameDotEdge": "Un nombre no puede empezar ni terminar con un punto.",
